WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.932
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.232 --> 00:00:08.886
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.186 --> 00:00:14.160
Unit two: Present Simple. Today you will talk about habits and routines.

4
00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:17.159
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:21.739
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.583 --> 00:00:23.492
Every day.

7
00:00:24.483 --> 00:00:27.156
Every day means each day, without missing one.

8
00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:29.308
I study every day.

9
00:00:29.917 --> 00:00:32.488
Your turn. Say: Every day.

10
00:00:35.333 --> 00:00:36.497
Every day.

11
00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:38.216
Always.

12
00:00:39.217 --> 00:00:42.029
Always means all the time, every time.

13
00:00:42.617 --> 00:00:44.280
She always smiles.

14
00:00:44.883 --> 00:00:47.245
Your turn. Say: Always.

15
00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:51.229
Always.

16
00:00:51.983 --> 00:00:53.008
Usually.

17
00:00:54.017 --> 00:00:55.923
Usually means most of the time.

18
00:00:56.517 --> 00:00:58.249
We usually eat at six.

19
00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:01.351
Your turn. Say: Usually.

20
00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:05.166
Usually.

21
00:01:05.917 --> 00:01:06.639
Play.

22
00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:09.650
Play means to do something for fun.

23
00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:11.565
They play football.

24
00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:14.361
Your turn. Say: Play.

25
00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:17.899
Play.

26
00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:19.430
Work.

27
00:01:20.417 --> 00:01:22.939
Work means to do a job or a task.

28
00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:25.283
My father works in a shop.

29
00:01:25.883 --> 00:01:27.886
Your turn. Say: Work.

30
00:01:30.733 --> 00:01:31.456
Work.

31
00:01:32.217 --> 00:01:33.102
Study.

32
00:01:34.117 --> 00:01:36.917
Study means to learn something from books or lessons.

33
00:01:37.517 --> 00:01:38.843
I study English.

34
00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:42.160
Your turn. Say: Study.

35
00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:45.873
Study.

36
00:01:46.617 --> 00:01:47.339
Sleep.

37
00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:51.185
Sleep means to rest with your eyes closed at night.

38
00:01:51.783 --> 00:01:53.400
Babies sleep a lot.

39
00:01:53.983 --> 00:01:56.914
Your turn. Say: Sleep.

40
00:01:59.767 --> 00:02:00.733
Sleep.

41
00:02:01.483 --> 00:02:02.241
Habit.

42
00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:05.609
Habit means something you do again and again.

43
00:02:06.217 --> 00:02:07.682
Reading is a good habit.

44
00:02:08.283 --> 00:02:10.529
Your turn. Say: Habit.

45
00:02:13.367 --> 00:02:14.112
Habit.

46
00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:18.946
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:19.783 --> 00:02:23.051
Visal, what do you do every day? Tell me one thing.

48
00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:29.809
I study English every day. I play football after school, and I sleep at ten o'clock.

49
00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:34.033
Good! What is the grammar in those sentences?

50
00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:41.590
It is the present simple. We use it for habits and routines. I play, you play, we play, they play.

51
00:02:42.683 --> 00:02:43.963
And with he or she?

52
00:02:45.050 --> 00:02:54.404
We add s: she plays, he works, it sleeps. After study we change y to ies: she studies. This is the most important rule.

53
00:02:55.567 --> 00:02:56.800
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:57.650 --> 00:03:01.530
Grammar focus: Present simple: verb (+ s).

55
00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:03.110
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:03.817 --> 00:03:05.630
I play football every day.

57
00:03:06.517 --> 00:03:07.831
She works in the morning.

58
00:03:08.717 --> 00:03:10.496
They always study before dinner.

59
00:03:11.433 --> 00:03:19.429
Use the present simple for habits and routines. Add s with he, she and it. Time words like every day, always and usually go with it.

60
00:03:20.183 --> 00:03:23.625
Be careful! Don't say: She play football every day.

61
00:03:25.567 --> 00:03:28.402
Say: She plays football every day.

62
00:03:28.702 --> 00:03:30.330
Add s with he, she and it.

63
00:03:31.133 --> 00:03:33.716
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:36.070
My Daily Habits.

65
00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:38.625
Every day, I wake up at six o'clock.

66
00:03:39.633 --> 00:03:41.761
I usually eat rice for breakfast.

67
00:03:42.767 --> 00:03:46.159
My mother works in a hospital, and my father works in a shop.

68
00:03:47.167 --> 00:03:49.468
We always study together after school.

69
00:03:50.467 --> 00:03:53.616
At ten o'clock, I sleep, because sleep is a good habit.

70
00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:58.609
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:01.357
She blank English every day.

72
00:04:01.657 --> 00:04:05.206
A, study. B, studies. C, studying.

73
00:04:08.767 --> 00:04:10.743
The answer is B: studies.

74
00:04:11.883 --> 00:04:13.720
They blank football on Sunday.

75
00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:17.778
A, plays. B, play. C, playing.

76
00:04:21.333 --> 00:04:23.124
The answer is B: play.

77
00:04:24.283 --> 00:04:25.911
'Every day' means blank.

78
00:04:26.211 --> 00:04:30.016
A, each day. B, never. C, one time.

79
00:04:33.567 --> 00:04:35.740
The answer is A: each day.

80
00:04:36.883 --> 00:04:38.500
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:43.812
A, He work in a bank.. B, He works in a bank.. C, He working in a bank..

82
00:04:47.367 --> 00:04:50.191
The answer is B: He works in a bank..

83
00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:54.441
According to the reading, what do they always do after school?

84
00:04:54.741 --> 00:04:58.719
A, sleep. B, study together. C, play football.

85
00:05:02.267 --> 00:05:04.429
The answer is B: study together.

86
00:05:05.633 --> 00:05:09.052
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:09.917 --> 00:05:12.148
What is one thing you always do every day?

88
00:05:20.950 --> 00:05:22.415
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:22.715 --> 00:05:37.447
I always brush my teeth every day. I do it in the morning and at night. This is a good habit because it keeps my teeth strong and healthy. I use the present simple to talk about it: I brush my teeth every day.

90
00:05:37.747 --> 00:05:39.492
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:40.383 --> 00:05:45.706
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and present simple: verb (+ s).

92
00:05:46.006 --> 00:05:50.713
Today's value is discipline. Follow your routine, even when it is hard.

93
00:05:51.013 --> 00:05:53.654
See you in Unit three. Goodbye!

94
00:05:53.954 --> 00:05:57.524
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

